<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hailu Tekle Haymanot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hailu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tekle-haymanot-saint">Tekle Haymanot</a> was an Ethiopian nobleman, son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tekle-haymanot-of-gojjam">Tekle Haymanot of Gojjam</a>, who governed Gojjam with the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras">Ras</a> and became one of the richest lords of the empire. In 1932 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> arrested him for helping the deposed emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iyasu-v">Lij Iyasu</a> escape, and he lost his province. He later collaborated with the Italian occupation.</p></div>
